<newsitem itemid="59652" id="root" date="1996-09-17" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Sears H1 profit 28 mln stg before charges.</title>
<headline>Sears H1 profit 28 mln stg before charges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to July 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) adjusted   1.4		    vs 1.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.05		   vs 1.05</p>
<p> Pretax preexceps	 28.0		   up 3.7 pct</p>
<p> Turnover		   908.4		  vs 1,062.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 23.00 to 27.00 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 29.0		   vs 30.3</p>
<p> Exceptional provisions 32.5		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.0		    vs nil</p>
<p> Tax			  2.0		    vs 7.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.5		    vs 22.1</p>
<p> Attributable	     0.1		    vs 21.7</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 5</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Profit before tax and after exceptionals was 2.5 million stg against 29.9 million last time.</p>
<p>The 32.5 million stg provision was principally to cover the cost of property disposals and debts owed by collapsed retailer Facia which Sears does not expect to recover. This is partly offset by the release of 7.5 million stg of disposal provisions from the previous financial year no longer needed, making total net additional provisions of 25.0 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
